Subject: net: mediatek: join the roaming receiver before releasing its socket

The self-rearming system work item blocks indefinitely in recvmsg, and remove
releases its socket without cancelling or joining the receiver. A failed bind
also leaves a dangling global socket pointer. Use a stoppable kthread with an
explicit queue/stop wait condition and a nonblocking recvmsg, then join before
release. Publish the socket only after bind and thread creation both succeed.

Validate every complete neighbour message and MAC attribute. The old parser
subtracts NLMSG_HDRLEN twice and can miss a minimal legal FDB notification;
short ndmsg and LLADDR payloads were read without their minimum size checks.
Keep the existing neighbour group, port ID, buffer size and FDB event semantics.

